Organize all the campers who already have levels into groups up to 5 or 6 for all 6 periods
Then I go person by person for each period so I do not miss anyone or make a mistake. I try to keep it even based on how many guarding periods someone has and how many lessons and how often they are in and out of the water but it is never perfect. 
The mornings are hard because I do not have many lessons, I try to have counselors take turns per week on who has to get into the water in the morning.
I have 2 people guarding rec if there are more than 10 swimmers, 3 if I have more than 15. MORNING ONLY. I have too many lessons in the afternoon to have 3 guards for rec or lessons.
I have 2 guard for lessons
 Usually  two or three people each morning period have to get in. I send at least 2-3 counselors a period to a sport
In the afternoon I give everybody two periods where they have to go into the water and either one period where they either are guarding or teach a lesson where they do not have to go in
I try to have 2 guards for lessons and 2 guards for rec. If there are less than 10 kids in rec, I only have 1 guard. Always two guards for lessons. 
I assign lessons based on skill level and ability of the counselor. 
James, Jack, Ethan, and JJ can teach levels 5 and 6. 
Hannah and Ariella can teach level 4
Everyone can teach levels 1-3
Levels 4-6 it is not required to get into the water
Levels 1-3 it is required to get into the water for the whole period 
On Mondays the campers who do not have a level are tested and given a level. I then adjust based on their level. I try to place them in a class with only 2-4 kids. If they have to go into a class that already has 5, I try to give a second counselor or split the class into two. Often the counselors who did the testing or I go back to the schedule and move things around. 


Additional context:
Levels are importable via a csv report (attached in prompt as context)
Swim staff will need an additional value in the schedule builder for the highest level they are able to teach
Swimmers are campers enrolled in either Rec Swim or Swim Lessons. 
Rec swim requires independant guards from Rec Swim.
A new view will be needed specifically for swim scheduling, this will need to act as a fully independant schedule from the main camp schedules. This scheduling will only ever apply to Swim staff.
An additional view will be needed for editing swim levels of campers enrolled in swim classes. This should be navigable while in the swim scheduling view.
An additional printable report will be needed that reports back all campers who were enrolled in Swim classes for a given session and their new swim levels
Each Level (1-6) has sub levels (Low 1, High 1, or 1)
